\\ Growth-pattern analysis of rank-jump fiber count vs log N.
\\
\\ We combine both surveys: low-N (N<=10^9) and high-N (10^9<N<=10^10).
\\ For each fiber we already know rank from survey outputs; here we just
\\ rebuild the conductor list and bin by log N.

default(parisize, 800000000);
default(realprecision, 20);

\\ Data: rank-jump fibers (q, N, rank) — copied from survey outputs.
\\ Source of truth: survey.out + survey_high.out.

{
all_jumps = [
  \\ N<=10^9 (54 fibers)
  [20/21, 4305, 1], [7/24, 22134, 1], [11/60, 82005, 2], [48/55, 237930, 1],
